{
  "concept": "backend-snapshot",
  "source": "recorded",
  "regenerate": "tools/herdr-probe/probe lifecycle agent-states",
  "why": "session.snapshot is where the mirror's world comes from - the first thing a connection reads and the thing every reconnect rebuilds from, since herdr offers no replay. The twin of backend-events.json, split from it because a response and a stream fail differently and a failure should say which one moved. The payloads are recorded snapshots except where a case is about a shape we have not seen and want to survive.",
