    {
      "name": "the transition counter is the highest stamp, not the number of agents",
      "why": "It is one session-wide counter (herdr src/app/actions.rs:2973), so panes carry interleaved values and the highest is what the session has run in total. Counting agents instead would make the gap check compare a total against a population and report a missed notification on every reconnect.",
      "given": {
        "snapshot": {
          "panes": [],
          "agents": [
            {
              "pane_id": "w1:p1",
              "state_change_seq": 2
            },
            {
              "pane_id": "w1:p5",
              "state_change_seq": 9
            },
            {
              "pane_id": "w1:p7",
              "state_change_seq": 4
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "workspaces": [],
        "tabs": [],
        "panes": [],
        "agentStates": {},
        "agents": {},
        "focus": {},
        "agentStateSeq": 9,
        "dropped": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a daemon with nothing open is an empty session, not a failure",
      "why": "What a freshly started herdr answers. Rendering it as broken would send someone debugging a connection that is working perfectly; whether the daemon is reachable is Health, and this is not that.",
      "given": {
        "snapshot": {
          "protocol": 19,
          "version": "0.8.0"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "workspaces": [],
        "tabs": [],
        "panes": [],
        "agentStates": {},
        "agents": {},
        "focus": {},
        "agentStateSeq": null,
        "dropped": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "one unreadable pane costs that pane and is counted",
      "why": "Same principle as a bad line on the stream: a session should survive one entry herdr changed. Counting them is what stops the survival from being silent - a mirror quietly one pane short looks exactly like a user who closed one.",
      "given": {
        "snapshot": {
          "panes": [
            {
              "pane_id": "w1:p1",
              "tab_id": "w1:t1",
              "workspace_id": "w1",
              "agent_status": "idle"
            },
            {
              "pane_id": "w1:p2",
              "workspace_id": "w1",
              "agent_status": "idle"
            },
            {
              "pane_id": "",
              "tab_id": "w1:t1",
              "workspace_id": "w1",
              "agent_status": "idle"
            }
          ],
          "tabs": [
            {
              "tab_id": "w1:t1",
              "workspace_id": "w1",
              "label": "1"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "workspaces": [],
        "tabs": [
          "w1:t1"
        ],
        "panes": [
          "w1:p1"
        ],
        "agentStates": {
          "w1:p1": "idle"
        },
        "agents": {},
        "focus": {},
        "agentStateSeq": null,
        "dropped": 2
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a focus cursor herdr did not state is unset, not empty",
      "why": "The mirror reads an unset cursor as saying nothing about that level. An empty string would be a cursor naming a pane that cannot exist, and every reader would have to handle the dangling case that the one who forgets renders as a missing pane.",
      "given": {
        "snapshot": {
          "panes": [],
          "focused_workspace_id": "w1",
          "focused_tab_id": "",
          "focused_pane_id": null
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "workspaces": [],
        "tabs": [],
        "panes": [],
        "agentStates": {},
        "agents": {},
        "focus": {
          "workspace": "w1"
        },
        "agentStateSeq": null,
        "dropped": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "an agent status herdr invented since this build reads as unknown",
      "why": "The snapshot path needs the same failing-closed as the event path, because a reconnect runs through here. Reading a new state as idle would tell the user nothing needs them, which is the one answer worse than showing nothing.",
      "given": {
        "snapshot": {
          "panes": [
            {
              "pane_id": "w1:p1",
              "tab_id": "w1:t1",
              "workspace_id": "w1",
              "agent_status": "compacting"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "workspaces": [],
        "tabs": [],
        "panes": [
          "w1:p1"
        ],
        "agentStates": {
          "w1:p1": "unknown"
        },
        "agents": {},
        "focus": {},
        "agentStateSeq": null,
        "dropped": 0
      }
    }
